"""Collect and normalize AI subscription limits for the Plasma widget.

The helper uses the same local sign-ins as the vendor CLIs: Codex's OAuth file,
GitHub CLI's credential store, and Claude Code's OAuth login, which is read
through the usage endpoint behind Claude Code's own /usage. The status-line
bridge is only a fallback for Claude logins this helper cannot read, and its
cached values are reported as stale rather than refreshed.

It ships inside the widget package so a KDE Store install needs nothing on
PATH, and it is also installed to ~/.local/bin by CMake for command-line use.

No credentials are printed or sent to the QML applet. The Codex and Copilot
endpoints are vendor-client endpoints rather than stable public APIs; failures
remain visible as an explicit state instead of becoming a fake zero.
"""

